    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
